        "eyebrow": "Soluble vs insoluble",
        "heading": "Not all cranberry <em>is equal.</em>",
        "body": "<p>Many products claim to have PACs, but if sourced from insoluble cranberry pomace (seeds, stems, skin, pulp), they remain trapped in fibre and cannot be absorbed by the body⁶˒⁷.</p><p>A controlled human study found that supplements made from juice-derived, soluble PACs produced significantly higher urinary anti-adhesion activity than supplements made mainly from whole fruit or pomace⁶.</p>",
